{"title":"Minimum Operations To Reduce An Integer To 0","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given a positive integer n, you can do the following operation any number of times:\n\nAdd or subtract a power of 2 from n.\n\nReturn the minimum number of operations to make n equal to 0.\nA number x is power of 2 if x == 2^i where i >= 0.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 39\nOutput: 3\n```\n\nExplanation: We can do the following operations:\n- Add 2^0 = 1 to n, so now n = 40.\n- Subtract 2^3 = 8 from n, so now n = 32.\n- Subtract 2^5 = 32 from n, so now n = 0.\nIt can be shown that 3 is the minimum number of operations we need to make n equal to 0.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 54\nOutput: 3\n```\n\nExplanation: We can do the following operations:\n- Add 2^1 = 2 to n, so now n = 56.\n- Add 2^3 = 8 to n, so now n = 64.\n- Subtract 2^6 = 64 from n, so now n = 0.\nSo the minimum number of operations is 3.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= n <= 10^5","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def minOperations(self, n: int) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().minOperations","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[1],"expected":1},{"input":[10],"expected":2},{"input":[100],"expected":3},{"input":[1030],"expected":3},{"input":[10365],"expected":5},{"input":[10519],"expected":6},{"input":[10545],"expected":6},{"input":[10581],"expected":7},{"input":[10663],"expected":7},{"input":[10797],"expected":7},{"input":[10941],"expected":7},{"input":[10966],"expected":7},{"input":[11],"expected":3},{"input":[11098],"expected":7},{"input":[11394],"expected":5},{"input":[1167],"expected":4},{"input":[11774],"expected":4},{"input":[11956],"expected":6},{"input":[11998],"expected":5},{"input":[12],"expected":2},{"input":[12011],"expected":6},{"input":[12226],"expected":4},{"input":[12283],"expected":4},{"input":[12430],"expected":5},{"input":[12817],"expected":5},{"input":[12856],"expected":5},{"input":[12946],"expec